@startuml specs-component-map
!theme plain

' ===========================================================================
' ChapterDesk / Chapterly — component map for the spec documentation.
'
' Purpose: one anchor diagram that a document about the specs can refer to.
'   * every node has a STABLE ALIAS (e.g. SVC_CHAT, ORCH_RUNNER) that the
'     text can use instead of repeating folder names;
'   * the third label line names the spec file whose assertions describe
'     that component (`(x.spec)`). Components covered only indirectly carry
'     "via <spec>" so the document can say why there is no own spec;
'   * arrows are the dependency direction used when picking a sequence
'     diagram: presentation → domain → LLM → data access → runtime.
'
' Render: plantuml docs/specs/component-map.puml   (SVG/PNG next to it)
' ===========================================================================

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam packageTitleAlignment left
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam NodePadding 12
hide stereotype

' Left-to-right keeps the dependency direction readable (presentation →
' domain → LLM → data access → runtime) and gives a ~1:1 aspect ratio that
' still embeds in a page. Without it the same graph renders ~7800x2100.
left to right direction

title ChapterDesk — component map for the spec documents

package "Bootstrap & routing" as BOOT {
  component "AppShell\napp.ts · app.html\n(app.spec)" as APP
  component "Routes\napp.routes.ts\n(no spec — asserted via page specs)" as ROUTES
}

